    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`POST /api/owners` now rejects with **409 Conflict** when the request's city already contains **50 or more** owners. Following the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md, I added a new pipeline step mirroring the existing `CheckUnique*` checks:\n\n- **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** (`.../function/owner/`) \u2014 reads the request via `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, counts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed, same normalization the household check uses), and throws the checked `CityAtCapacityException` once the count reaches 50. It runs before `BuildOwner`, so no owner is created on conflict.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** (`extends Exception`) and **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** (responds 409 with `{\"errors\":[\"city\"]}`), matching the `DuplicateTelephone`/`DuplicateHousehold` handlers.\n- **Escalation YAML** `.../escalation/...CityAtCapacityException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n- **Wired the step** into `owners.POST.yml` as `checkCityCapacity`, inserted between `checkHousehold` and `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbours.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe pre-existing acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, expects the 51st to be `409`) now passes, and the full suite is **BUILD SUCCESS** (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
